SOAPBOX: Thanks to Ray, W2RE for making his wonderful remote station in Summit, NY available for use in this contest.
SOAPBOX: All operators were youth: Mason, KM4SII (17), Charles, AA4LS (13) and Connor, W4IPC (18).
SOAPBOX: We operated SO1R with Connor operating the beginning and end of the contest, and Mason operating the middle period (after finishing his SAT exam Saturday morning) and Charles operating in between.
SOAPBOX: The station performed well, especially on the high bands. The bands themselves weren't terrible, but also can't be classified as overly exceptional either.
SOAPBOX: While FT4 did at times produce higher  rates,   all
SOAPBOX: An intense thunderstorm came directly over the station causing a period of extreme QRN and rain static, but fortunately it cleared up soon after.
SOAPBOX: Apart from that period, mother nature left us alone.
SOAPBOX: Again, thanks to Ray W2RE and the Remote Ham Radio Youth Program for the use of the great remote station. http://www.w2re.com/summit/ https://www.remotehamradio.com/youth/
SOAPBOX: Thanks to everyone who called us!
SOAPBOX: 73 Mason, KM4SII and Connor, W4IPC
